\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 When your Spring Boot backend receives an uploaded file, it executes the following atomic database transaction sequence to keep the architecture smooth:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Initialize Run:
\f0\b0  Inserts an 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 upload_details
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  record with a status of 
\fs30 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 'PROCESSING'
